operation countSetBitsInSignedInt64
input operation countSetBitsInSignedInt64 inputValue CSignedInt64
output operation countSetBitsInSignedInt64 CSignedInt64
memory countSetBitsInSignedInt64 heap no
async countSetBitsInSignedInt64 no
purpose operation countSetBitsInSignedInt64 "Returns the population count of inputValue (number of 1-bits in its full 64-bit two's-complement representation). Correct for negative inputs: countSetBitsInSignedInt64(-1) == 64."
invariant operation countSetBitsInSignedInt64 "For inputValue >= 0, inspects each bit via modulo-2 on a halving working value. For inputValue < 0, applies popcount(n) == 64 - popcount(-n - 1) so the sign-extension bits are counted (arithmetic divide-by-two toward zero would otherwise drop them)."
guarantee countSetBitsInSignedInt64 "Total â€” in [0, 64]."
label startCountSetBitsInSignedInt64
storage module immutable zeroPc I64 0
storage module immutable onePc I64 1
storage module immutable twoPc I64 2
storage module immutable limitPc I64 64
storage module immutable negOnePc I64 -1
memory countSetBitsInSignedInt64 mutable pcVal I64 0
set memory pcVal inputValue
memory countSetBitsInSignedInt64 mutable pcWasNegativeFlag I64 0
memory countSetBitsInSignedInt64 mutable pcCount I64 0
memory countSetBitsInSignedInt64 mutable pcIter I64 0
# Negative inputs: arithmetic divide-by-two (toward zero) collapses a
# negative value's sign-extension bits, so the raw loop would undercount.
# Use popcount(n) == 64 - popcount(-n - 1) for n < 0: `-n - 1` is
# non-negative for every negative n (and wraps to INT64_MAX for INT64_MIN,
# which is still correct), so the unsigned loop below counts it exactly.
call pcDetectNegativeCall math.lessThanI64
argument pcDetectNegativeCall left I64 inputValue
argument pcDetectNegativeCall right I64 zeroPc
run pcDetectNegativeCall
bind value pcInputIsNegative Bool pcDetectNegativeCall
branch if condition pcInputIsNegative target pcPrepareNegative
branch else target pcLoop
label pcPrepareNegative
set memory pcWasNegativeFlag onePc
call pcNegateInputCall math.multiplyI64
argument pcNegateInputCall left I64 inputValue
argument pcNegateInputCall right I64 negOnePc
run pcNegateInputCall
bind value pcNegatedInput I64 pcNegateInputCall
call pcComplementSourceCall math.subtractI64
argument pcComplementSourceCall left I64 pcNegatedInput
argument pcComplementSourceCall right I64 onePc
run pcComplementSourceCall
bind value pcComplementSource I64 pcComplementSourceCall
set memory pcVal pcComplementSource
jump target pcLoop
label pcLoop
call popcountDoneCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
argument popcountDoneCall left I64 pcIter
argument popcountDoneCall right I64 limitPc
run popcountDoneCall
bind value popcountDoneCallB Bool popcountDoneCall
branch if condition popcountDoneCallB target pcReturn
call popcountModCall math.moduloI64
argument popcountModCall left I64 pcVal
argument popcountModCall right I64 twoPc
run popcountModCall
bind value pcBit I64 popcountModCall
call popcountBitNonzeroCall math.notEqualI64
argument popcountBitNonzeroCall left I64 pcBit
argument popcountBitNonzeroCall right I64 zeroPc
run popcountBitNonzeroCall
bind value pcSet Bool popcountBitNonzeroCall
branch if condition pcSet target popcountIncrementBranch
branch else target pcAdvance
label popcountIncrementBranch
call popcountIncrementCall math.addI64
argument popcountIncrementCall left I64 pcCount
argument popcountIncrementCall right I64 onePc
run popcountIncrementCall
bind value pcNext I64 popcountIncrementCall
set memory pcCount pcNext
jump target pcAdvance
label pcAdvance
call popcountDivideCall math.divideI64
argument popcountDivideCall left I64 pcVal
argument popcountDivideCall right I64 twoPc
run popcountDivideCall
bind value pcHalved I64 popcountDivideCall
set memory pcVal pcHalved
call popcountIterIncrementCall math.addI64
argument popcountIterIncrementCall left I64 pcIter
argument popcountIterIncrementCall right I64 onePc
run popcountIterIncrementCall
bind value pcIterNext I64 popcountIterIncrementCall
set memory pcIter pcIterNext
jump target pcLoop
label pcReturn
call pcWasNegativeCheckCall math.equalI64
argument pcWasNegativeCheckCall left I64 pcWasNegativeFlag
argument pcWasNegativeCheckCall right I64 onePc
run pcWasNegativeCheckCall
bind value pcWasNegativeResult Bool pcWasNegativeCheckCall
branch if condition pcWasNegativeResult target pcReturnComplement
return value pcCount
label pcReturnComplement
call pcFinalComplementCall math.subtractI64
argument pcFinalComplementCall left I64 limitPc
argument pcFinalComplementCall right I64 pcCount
run pcFinalComplementCall
bind value pcComplementedCount CSignedInt64 pcFinalComplementCall
return value pcComplementedCount

operation countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64
input operation countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64 inputValue CSignedInt64
output operation countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64 CSignedInt64
memory countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64 heap no
async countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64 no
purpose operation countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64 "Returns the count of trailing zero bits in inputValue's 64-bit representation. Returns 64 for inputValue == 0 (matching GCC __builtin_ctzll)."
invariant operation countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64 "Halves the value while the low bit is zero, counting iterations. Zero input short-circuits to 64."
guarantee countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64 "Total."
label startCountTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64
storage module immutable zeroTz I64 0
storage module immutable oneTz I64 1
storage module immutable twoTz I64 2
storage module immutable sixtyFourTz I64 64
# Special case n == 0
call ctzEqualZeroCall math.equalI64
argument ctzEqualZeroCall left I64 inputValue
argument ctzEqualZeroCall right I64 zeroTz
run ctzEqualZeroCall
bind value nIsZero Bool ctzEqualZeroCall
branch if condition nIsZero target tzReturn64
memory countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64 mutable tzVal I64 0
set memory tzVal inputValue
memory countTrailingZeroBitsInSignedInt64 mutable tzCount I64 0
label tzLoop
call tzModCall math.moduloI64
argument tzModCall left I64 tzVal
argument tzModCall right I64 twoTz
run tzModCall
bind value tzMod I64 tzModCall
call ctzBitSetCall math.notEqualI64
argument ctzBitSetCall left I64 tzMod
argument ctzBitSetCall right I64 zeroTz
run ctzBitSetCall
bind value tzSet Bool ctzBitSetCall
branch if condition tzSet target tzReturn
call tzDivCall math.divideI64
argument tzDivCall left I64 tzVal
argument tzDivCall right I64 twoTz
run tzDivCall
bind value tzNext I64 tzDivCall
set memory tzVal tzNext
call tzIncCall math.addI64
argument tzIncCall left I64 tzCount
argument tzIncCall right I64 oneTz
run tzIncCall
bind value tzCountNext I64 tzIncCall
set memory tzCount tzCountNext
jump target tzLoop
label tzReturn
return value tzCount
label tzReturn64
return value sixtyFourTz

operation signOfSignedInt64
input operation signOfSignedInt64 inputValue CSignedInt64
output operation signOfSignedInt64 CSignedInt64
memory signOfSignedInt64 heap no
async signOfSignedInt64 no
purpose operation signOfSignedInt64 "Returns -1 when inputValue is negative, 1 when positive, 0 when zero."
guarantee signOfSignedInt64 "Total â€” result is always exactly -1, 0, or 1."
label startSignOfSignedInt64
storage module immutable zeroSi I64 0
storage module immutable oneSi I64 1
storage module immutable negOneSi I64 -1
call absDiffLessThanCall math.lessThanI64
argument absDiffLessThanCall left I64 inputValue
argument absDiffLessThanCall right I64 zeroSi
